1) SSH 登录用 top -H 定位占用最高的进程与线程；\n2) 用 pe:
1) SSH in and use top -H to find the busiest processes and threads;
2) Use perf top or a language profiler to find the hot functions;
3) Tell business growth apart from a code fault (infinite loop, frequent GC);
4) For growth, change to a larger flavour in the console or scale out horizontally.

1) 在华为云控制台看该 DCS 实例的监控曲线确认趋势；\n2) 用 redi:
1) Check that DCS instance's monitoring curves in the Huawei Cloud console;
2) Connect with redis-cli and run INFO to confirm the real state of the relevant metric;
3) Once the cause is identified, follow the usual Redis path (big keys, slow commands, connection leaks);
4) If capacity is short, change the instance flavour in the console.

1) 在华为云控制台看该 ELB 的带宽监控曲线，确认是持续增长还是突发；\n2:
1) Check that ELB's bandwidth monitoring curve in the console to tell sustained growth from a spike;
2) Determine whether it is normal business growth or abnormal traffic (crawlers, attacks);
3) For genuine growth, adjust the ELB specification or bandwidth cap in the console;
4) For abnormal traffic, use WAF/DDoS protection to rate limit or block.

1) 在华为云控制台确认实例与 broker 状态；\n2) 确认客户端是否已自:
1) Confirm the instance and broker state in the Huawei Cloud console;
2) Confirm clients have failed over to other brokers — with multiple brokers only some partitions are unavailable;
3) If the console looks fine but clients report errors, check the network and security groups plus the client's nameserver address;
4) If it stays unavailable, open a ticket with Huawei Cloud.

1) 在控制台定位是哪个节点 CPU 高；\n2) 集群模式下通常是数据倾斜——:
1) Identify the node with high CPU in the console;
2) In cluster mode this is usually data skew — a hot key in one slot, findable with --hotkeys;
3) Hot keys can be mitigated with a local cache or by splitting the key;
4) If it stays high after rebalancing, upgrade the flavour.

1) 在控制台的后端服务器组里定位健康检查失败的实例；\n2) 登录该实例确认应:
1) In the console's backend server group, find the instances failing the health check;
2) Log in to that instance and confirm the application process and port are alive;
3) If the application is fine, verify the health check configuration (path, port, timeout, interval) matches reality;
4) Confirm the remaining healthy instances can carry the traffic and scale out immediately if not.

1) 在控制台看流控发生的时间点，对照带宽与 QPS 曲线确认是哪一项超限；\n:
1) Check when the throttling occurred in the console and compare against the bandwidth and QPS curves to see which limit was exceeded;
2) For bandwidth, use --bigkeys to find and split large keys;
3) For QPS, add a local cache or batch requests on the application side;
4) If you genuinely need more capacity, change the instance flavour in the console.

1) 在控制台看消息堆积量——堆积会显著占用内存；\n2) 优先恢复消费把堆积清:
1) Check the message backlog in the console — a backlog consumes significant memory;
2) Restoring consumption to drain the backlog is the most direct fix;
3) Check whether the message retention period is set too long;
4) For sustained growth, upgrade the instance flavour.

1) 在控制台看该 ELB 的连接数监控，确认增长趋势；\n2) 确认后端服务是:
1) Check that ELB's connection count monitoring in the console for the growth trend;
2) Check whether the backend is responding more slowly and causing connections to pile up — a high connection count is often a symptom of a slow backend rather than the cause;
3) If the backend is fine, upgrade the ELB specification for the growth;
4) Check whether clients are failing to reuse connections.

1) 在控制台看该 broker 的 TPS 与消息堆积曲线，确认是生产还是消费:
1) Check that broker's TPS and message backlog curves in the console to tell producer-side from consumer-side pressure;
2) For a heavy consume backlog, scale out consumers first;
3) For a produce spike, evaluate upgrading the instance flavour;
4) Confirm no oversized messages or huge batch sends are overwhelming the broker.

1) 用 CLIENT LIST 按来源统计，定位频繁重连的客户端；\n2) 应:
1) Use CLIENT LIST grouped by source to find the clients reconnecting frequently;
2) Switching the application to a connection pool with reused connections is the real fix;
3) Check whether the client's connection timeout is set too short and causing repeated reconnects;
4) Confirm no throttling or memory alarm is causing the server to close connections.

1) 用 INFO stats 看 instantaneous_input_kb:
1) Use INFO stats to check instantaneous_input_kbps / output_kbps and determine the direction;
2) Use redis-cli --bigkeys to find large keys — reading and writing large keys is the most common cause of saturated bandwidth;
3) Split large keys and reduce one-shot bulk reads;
4) If you genuinely need more bandwidth, upgrade the flavour in the console.

1) 用 SLOWLOG GET 10 找耗时最高的命令；\n2) 重点排查 K:
1) Run SLOWLOG GET 10 to find the slowest commands;
2) Focus on O(N) commands such as KEYS, HGETALL and SMEMBERS and on big-key operations, switching to SCAN or batching;
3) Check whether an RDB/AOF persistence run is causing the CPU spike;
4) If it stays high after tuning, upgrade the instance flavour in the console.

1) 用 SLOWLOG GET 10 看具体慢命令与耗时；\n2) 重点排查:
1) Run SLOWLOG GET 10 for the specific slow commands and their timings;
2) Focus on O(N) commands and big-key operations;
3) Switching to SCAN with batching and splitting large keys is the real fix;
4) If the slow commands come from a scheduled job, move it to off-peak hours.

1) 用 chronyc tracking 确认偏移与上游源状态；\n2) 华为:
1) Run chronyc tracking to check the offset and upstream source state;
2) Huawei Cloud ECS should use the internal NTP service (ntp.myhuaweicloud.com) — confirm it is configured;
3) Start chronyd if it is not running and enable it at boot;
4) For a large offset, use chronyc makestep to step the clock.

1) 用 df -h 定位挂载点，用 du -x --max-depth=1 找:
1) Run df -h to find the mount point and du -x --max-depth=1 for the largest directories;
2) Clean logs and temporary files first, and use lsof +L1 for deleted-but-unreleased files;
3) Expand the EVS disk online in the console, then use growpart plus resize2fs/xfs_growfs to grow the filesystem;
4) Longer term, evaluate moving the data directory to a dedicated cloud disk.

1) 用 df -i 确认挂载点；\n2) 逐层统计文件数找出小文件最多的目录；:
1) Run df -i to find the mount point;
2) Count files level by level to find the directories with the most small files;
3) Common sources are log fragments, session files and container layers — confirm and bulk delete;
4) Longer term, consider moving small-file workloads to a dedicated partition.

1) 用 free -h 确认 available 与 swap 使用；\n2):
1) Run free -h to check available memory and swap;
2) Run ps aux --sort=-%mem | head to find the largest consumer and judge whether it is leaking;
3) For a leak, capture a heap in the application — a restart alone is not enough;
4) For growth, change to a larger memory flavour in the console.

1) 用 iostat -x 1 确认实际 IOPS 与 await；\n2):
1) Run iostat -x 1 to check actual IOPS and await;
2) Run iotop -oP to find the process writing the most;
3) Compare against the EVS disk type's IOPS ceiling to see whether it has topped out — ultra-high performance and general purpose disks differ greatly;
4) If it has, upgrade the disk type or expand it in the console (IOPS usually scales linearly with capacity); if not, optimise the application's write pattern.

